---
layout: layouts/base.njk
page_id: problems
page_width: medium
title: Sleep problems
eyebrow: Step 2
heading: What's keeping you up?
# The lede under the H1. `lede_tools` describes the filter and the group
# buttons, which need JavaScript, so it shows only once problems.js has shown
# them. It stays the same in both views, so it names both kinds of group
# (Problems-A: "Open an area to see its topics, ..."). `lede` is true either
# way. Together they are the meta description.
lede_tools: Open an area or a time of day to see its topics, or search in your own words.
lede: Choose as many as sound like you.
eleventyComputed:
  summary: "{{ lede_tools }} {{ lede }}"
styles: ["pages/problems.css"]
scripts: ["problems.js"]
# The "When it happens" groups, in display order. The ids are the
# time_of_day values in scripts/validate-content.js (TIMES_OF_DAY; a test
# keeps the two lists in step), and the build fails on a problem whose
# time_of_day isn't here (groupByTime in eleventy.config.js).
time_groups:
  - { id: evening, name: "In the evening" }
  - { id: bedtime, name: "At bedtime" }
  - { id: night, name: "During the night" }
  - { id: early-morning, name: "Early morning" }
  - { id: day, name: "During the day" }
  - { id: any, name: "Any time" }
---
{#-
  Sleep problems (/problems/): SPEC §7.2, §8.1; HANDOFF §6.3; boards
  Problems-A.dc.html and Problems-Phone.dc.html, with the changes in SPEC
  §7.5 (the slider toggle, no "Open all areas", "When it happens" grouped
  like the areas).

  This page renders its own <main> and title band (on layouts/base.njk, not
  page.njk) because the filter, view toggle and result line sit inside the
  band. The band reuses the title-band classes from site.css.

  Two views of the same problems, built the same way (topicGroup below): By
  area, one group per area (the default), and "When it happens", one group
  per time of day. Each group is a plain <h2> with its name, the area's
  description and a count, over the list of its problems.

  Without JavaScript (SPEC §2, §11):
    - every area is open; the problem links are always reachable;
    - the toolbar (filter and view toggle), the lede's sentence about it and
      the "When it happens" view carry `hidden`, so no dead control is ever
      shown or described and no link is listed twice; the result line
      ("36 topics in 10 areas") stays, because it is true either way.
  src/js/problems.js turns each group heading's <span> into a
  <button aria-expanded aria-controls>, in both views, shows the toolbar,
  and runs the filter and the view switch. Hooks for it are data-*
  attributes; classes are for styling only.

  Analytics: this page sends no page_view (SPEC §10.2) and the filter sends
  nothing (§8.1), so there is no track_page_view here.

  Keywords: data/keywords.csv (SPEC §8.2, M2) becomes the global `keywords`.
  A problem's row, when there is one, is written to its list item's
  data-keywords in the By area view, where problems.js reads it for the
  filter; until the file exists nothing is written.
-#}
{%- from "partials/icons.njk" import icon -%}

{#- A problem's keywords from data/keywords.csv, or nothing. -#}
{%- macro keywordsFor(slug) -%}
{%- for row in keywords -%}{%- if row.page_id == slug -%}{{ row.keywords }}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- A link to a problem: short title (with the "New" pill), first-person
    line and an arrow. Built on .topic-card (components.css). The spaces
    between the spans keep the link's accessible name readable ("Tired but
    wired I'm tired, ..."). -#}
{%- macro topicCard(p) -%}
<a class="topic-card topic-card--row" href="{{ p.url }}">
  <span class="topic-card__text">
    <span class="topic-card__title"><span data-topic-title>{{ p.title }}</span>{% if p.isNew %} <span class="topic-card__new">New</span>{% endif %}</span>
    <span class="topic-card__statement" data-topic-statement>{{ p.statement }}</span>
  </span>
  {{ icon('arrow-right', 20, 'topic-card__arrow') }}
</a>
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- One group of problems, in either view: a plain <h2> (name, optional
    description, count and chevron) over its list, open. `sectionId` is set
    only for areas, so /problems/#core links to an area (SPEC §7.2); times
    of day have none, since "day" is both an area and a time of day.
    `withKeywords` writes data-keywords (By area only: problems.js reads
    each problem's words once). -#}
{%- macro topicGroup(sectionId, listId, name, description, problems, withKeywords) -%}
{%- set n = problems.length %}
<section class="group-list__group"{% if sectionId %} id="{{ sectionId }}"{% endif %}>
  <h2 class="group-list__heading">
    <span class="group-list__header" data-group-header>
      <span class="group-list__text">
        <span class="group-list__name" data-group-name>{{ name }}</span>
        {%- if description %}
        <span class="group-list__description">{{ description }}</span>
        {%- endif %}
      </span>
      <span class="group-list__count"><span data-group-count data-total="{{ n }}">{{ n }}</span><span class="group-list__count-unit"> {{ 'topic' if n == 1 else 'topics' }}</span></span>
      <span class="group-list__chevron" aria-hidden="true">{{ icon('chevron-down', 18) }}</span>
    </span>
  </h2>
  <ul class="group-list__problems" id="{{ listId }}" role="list" data-group-list>
    {%- for p in problems %}{% set kw = (keywordsFor(p.slug) | trim) if withKeywords else '' %}
    <li data-slug="{{ p.slug }}"{% if kw | length %} data-keywords="{{ kw }}"{% endif %}>{{ topicCard(p) }}</li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- set topicAreas = collections.problems | groupByArea(areas) -%}
{%- set topicTimes = collections.problems | groupByTime(time_groups) -%}
{%- set total = collections.problems.length -%}
<main id="main" class="problems-page">
  <div class="band on-dark problems-band">
    <div class="band__inner container">
      <p class="band__eyebrow">{{ eyebrow }}</p>
      <h1 class="band__title">{{ heading }}</h1>
      <p class="band__lede"><span data-problems-hint hidden>{{ lede_tools }} </span>{{ lede }}</p>
      {#- Shown by problems.js once its handlers are attached. No <form> and
          no name: nothing is submitted, stored or sent (SPEC §8.1).
          autocomplete="off" keeps typed health terms out of the browser's
          form history and stops a stale value or view being restored. #}
      <div class="problems-tools" data-problems-tools hidden>
        <div class="problems-search">
          {#- Not "Search sleep problems": that is the header's site search,
              which leaves the page. This field only narrows the list here. #}
          <label class="problems-search__label" for="problem-filter">Find a sleep problem on this page</label>
          <input class="problems-search__input" id="problem-filter" type="search" placeholder="Try: night sweats, 3am, partner" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" aria-describedby="problem-filter-status" data-problem-filter>
        </div>
        {#- Two native radios (one or the other, arrow keys, the legend read
            out), drawn as a slider: a pill-shaped track and a thumb that
            sits under the checked one's label. The track and thumb are
            empty, decorative spans after the radios, so the CSS can follow
            the radios' :checked and :focus-visible with sibling selectors;
            keep this order. #}
        <fieldset class="view-toggle">
          <legend class="visually-hidden">Group topics by</legend>
          <div class="view-toggle__options">
            <input class="view-toggle__input visually-hidden" type="radio" name="problems-view" id="view-area" value="area" checked autocomplete="off" data-view-choice>
            <label class="view-toggle__label" for="view-area">By area</label>
            <input class="view-toggle__input visually-hidden" type="radio" name="problems-view" id="view-time" value="time" autocomplete="off" data-view-choice>
            <label class="view-toggle__label" for="view-time">When it happens</label>
            <span class="view-toggle__track"></span>
            <span class="view-toggle__thumb"></span>
          </div>
        </fieldset>
      </div>
      <p class="problems-status" id="problem-filter-status" aria-live="polite" data-filter-status>{{ total }} topics in {{ topicAreas.length }} areas</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="page-body container">
    <div class="problems" data-problems>
      {#- By area (the default view). #}
      <div class="group-list" data-view-panel="area">
        {%- for area in topicAreas %}
        {{ topicGroup(area.area_id, 'area-' + area.area_id + '-problems', area.name, area.description, area.problems, true) }}
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>

      {#- When it happens: the same groups, one per time of day, with the
          problems in collection order (area, then order within the area).
          Shown only by problems.js (the control that chooses it needs
          JavaScript); without it the areas above already list every
          problem once. #}
      <div class="group-list" data-view-panel="time" hidden>
        {%- for time in topicTimes %}
        {{ topicGroup(null, 'time-' + time.id + '-problems', time.name, null, time.problems, false) }}
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>

      <div class="panel problems-nudge">
        <p class="problems-nudge__text">Haven't watched the introduction yet? It explains the ideas the other videos build on.</p>
        <p class="link-standalone"><a href="/start/">Go to the introduction</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>
